      "sourceTextSha256": "4295e1cf5e3a32f6ddcc14c0f57a0faf9eee0224d587cea62faa5cb685d6d273",
      "text": "Day 10 · After breakfast, shared tour of the Brazilian side of the falls with an English-speaking guide. On the border of Brazil, Argentina and Paraguay, within a national park of unique flora and fauna, 275 waterfalls, each with its own name, rush down into the canyon of the Devil’s Throat. Their name comes from the Tupi-Guarani for “big water”. The contrast between the calm, almost lazy river above the falls and the powerful, boiling torrents below is stunning: you could watch this spectacle for hours.",
